      "title": "Note",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Qwen-Edit-2511 Lightning \u2192 Z-Image Turbo refiner\n\n## Why this exists \u2014 measured, not assumed\n\nA Qwen edit pass VAE-encodes and regenerates the **whole frame**, not just the\nregion you asked about. Everything comes back softer. Laplacian variance\n(micro-detail proxy) on this box, 2026-08-26, same source image:\n\n| | laplacian-var | vs source |\n|---|---|---|\n| original photo | **67.8** | \u2014 |\n| Lightning 4-step | 32.0 | \u221253% |\n| 20-step CFG 4.0 | 31.1 | \u221254% |\n\n**Step count is not the lever.** 20 steps is marginally *worse* than 4 and takes\n4.5\u00d7 longer. The flattening is inherent to the edit pass, so the fix has to come\nafter it \u2014 which is what stage 2 is.\n\nRe-measure after any change you make:\n\n```\npython3 -c \"\nimport numpy as np;from PIL import Image\nfrom numpy.lib.stride_tricks import sliding_window_view as w\na=np.asarray(Image.open('OUT.png').convert('L'),float)\nk=np.array([[0,1,0],[1,-4,1],[0,1,0]],float)\nprint(((w(a,(3,3))*k).sum((-1,-2))).var())\"\n```\n\nHigher is sharper. Target: move 32 back toward 67.\n\n## Stage 2 \u2014 the refiner\n\n`VAEDecode` (Qwen VAE) \u2192 `VAEEncode` (ae.safetensors) \u2192 `KSampler` at **denoise 0.25**.\n\nThe round-trip through pixels is deliberate: it is the only clean way to hand an\nimage between two families whose latent spaces are not guaranteed to share a\nscale factor. The loss it costs is far smaller than the detail stage 2 rebuilds.\n\n**`denoise` is the whole control:**\n\n| value | effect |\n|---|---|\n| 0.05\u20130.15 | grade/micro-contrast only, identity untouched \u2014 the conservative range |\n| **0.25** | **shipped default** \u2014 rebuilds texture, keeps composition |\n| 0.35 | strong texture rebuild, starts drifting from the edit |\n| 0.50+ | the refiner is now re-imagining, not refining. Too far. |\n\n**Steps interact with denoise.** ComfyUI runs `steps \u00d7 denoise` actual steps, so\n`20 \u00d7 0.25` = **5 real steps** \u2014 right for a turbo model distilled\naround 8. If you lower denoise, raise steps to keep the effective count near 5\u20138,\nor the pass will be undercooked.\n\n**CFG stays 1.0.** Z-Image Turbo is guidance-distilled; the negative runs through\n`ConditioningZeroOut` and is never evaluated.\n\n## If the refiner eats your edit\n\nDrop `denoise` toward 0.15. If instead it is not fixing fur or skin, raise toward\n0.35. Judge by the laplacian number, not by feel \u2014 at 100% zoom everything looks\nsharper than it is.\n\n## Reading the output\n\nTwo image outputs: **Stage 1 (pre-refine)** preview and the saved **Stage 2**\nresult. Same run, same seed, so the comparison is honest.\n\n## Licence\n\n**Apache 2.0** \u2014 the safe default if commercial use matters.\n\n## The reference-method symmetry still applies\n\n`FluxKontextMultiReferenceLatentMethod` is on **both** conditioning branches. At\nCFG 1.0 it happens not to matter, but leaving it asymmetric plants a bug that\nonly appears if you ever raise CFG \u2014 pink speckling across flat areas. Measured\nhere on 2026-08-26.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
